In simple words:  Instead of manually logging into 100 servers and doing the same work, Ansible lets you do it from one machine.

Example
Suppose you have 3 servers:

              Ansible Control Node
                     |
          -----------------------
          |          |          |
       Server 1   Server 2   Server 3

You want to install Nginx on all 3 servers.

Without Ansible
You manually:
SSH → Server 1 → install nginx
SSH → Server 2 → install nginx
SSH → Server 3 → install nginx
--------------------------------------------- 
Ansible architecture
                 Ansible
              Control Node
                   |
        -----------------------
        |          |          |
       SSH        SSH        SSH
        |          |          |
     Server1    Server2    Server3

Ansible is generally agentless.
That means you normally don't install an Ansible agent on every managed Linux server only control node
