pip install ansible is a valid way to install Ansible, but being a Red Hat project does not mean you must use pip.
Ansible can be installed using different methods depending on the OS.

Recommended: dnf
For a normal RHEL installation, use:  sudo dnf install ansible-core -y
dnf is the Linux package manager for RHEL.   RHEL means Red Hat Enterprise Linux.

pip
You can also install Ansible through Python:  python3 -m pip install ansible
pip is the Python package manager, not the RHEL package manager.
